@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Use it when you want the text written as-is.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, does not word wrap or crop the output, does not interpret console markup, and does not replace emoji codes. It does support highlighting, controlled by the ``highlight`` argument (which defaults to ``True``), and a basic ``style`` argument. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[not bold] :smiley:", "foo", style="bold")
+
+Output still goes through the normal print pipeline, so it is buffered, flushed and captured like any other output.
+
+
